	'nl_l0' => 'The letter',
	'nl_l1' => 'Subscribe',
	'nl_lede' => 'The studio letter is published four times a year by Tsukuri Design Office. Each edition shares practical documentation from our model shop bench and notes on recent manufacturing launches.',
	'nl_n0' => 'Four times a year',
	'nl_n1' => 'Two parts',
	'nl_p0' => 'Four times a year, Tsukuri Design Office issues a quiet, carefully curated dispatch directly from our Haverholt workshop. We write for product directors, engineering leads, and medical device founders who value honest manufacturing insights over promotional agency rhetoric. The studio letter contains no sponsored content, no speculative design concepts, and no marketing clutter. Instead, each issue provides concise, transparent reflections on taking physical products from early hand-sanded foam blocks through to factory injection molding tools, drawing entirely from live cases encountered across our studio and model shop.',
	'nl_p1' => 'Every quarterly newsletter is structured around two substantive sections: one thoroughly documented finished case study and one technical note written directly from our model shop bench. In the case study review, we explain the ergonomic and engineering challenges behind a completed medical device or consumer product, detailing the number of foam iterations required and the tooling hurdles resolved during production. The model shop note, contributed by Kofi Asante, examines specific workshop techniques—such as sanding stick geometries, resin print tolerances, or surface texturing methods. Subscriptions can be managed or cancelled at any time by contacting studio@tsukuri.example.',
