	'pr_name' => 'What clients bring',
	'pr_p1' => 'A client usually arrives with a digital model that looked convincing on screen and a first sample that failed the moment someone held it. Screens hide the physical facts of weight, balance and edge. When a part is produced without being tested in a real hand, a small miscalculation in grip quietly undoes months of careful engineering.',
	'pr_p2' => 'The gap lives in small details that specifications overlook. A bedside button must be found by touch in a dark ward. A kettle lid must open with one wet hand without burning knuckles. A moulded casing must release from its tool without cracking the ribs inside it. None of this shows up in a drawing that tested well.',
	'pr_p3' => 'We close the gap with foam, people and the factory floor. We take at most nine projects a year, so the same eight designers and engineers stay with you from the first brief to the first-off sample. Real hands test every curve long before any steel is cut for tooling, and the factory is in the room early.',
