	'st_l1' => 'The people',
	'st_l2' => 'A day',
	'st_l3' => 'Why nine',
	'st_lede' => 'Founded in 2011 by Ines Varga, Tsukuri Design Office is an eight-person industrial design consultancy based in Haverholt. We limit our annual workload to at most nine projects to ensure dedicated senior involvement from initial foam exploration to factory production.',
	'st_p' => 'Every project starts with a discovery workshop: one full day at our studio or yours, and a written problem statement within 5 working days. The fee of €2,400 is deducted from the next stage if you go ahead. Write or call, and Paul replies within 3 working days with two dates.',
	'st_p0' => 'Tsukuri Design Office was established in 2011 by design director Ines Varga with a steadfast commitment to physical prototyping and careful manufacturing oversight. Over the past decade and a half, our practice has purposely remained an eight-person multidisciplinary studio operating out of Studio 4, Foundry Lane 18 in Haverholt. We deliberately accept no more than nine client projects each year, ensuring that no more than four programs occupy the tooling phase simultaneously. This strict capacity limit ensures that our most experienced designers personally sand the foam models, conduct clinical field observations, and stand beside tooling technicians on factory floors.',
	'st_p1' => 'Daily life inside our Haverholt studio follows a purposeful rhythm centered on physical verification. Each morning begins promptly at 09:00 with a collaborative model review gathered around the workshop bench, where the entire team critiques the previous day\'s foam studies and prints. Afternoons are dedicated to focused production CAD engineering, wall thickness studies, and supplier alignment calls. On Tuesdays, clinic and home visits take research team members into field environments to observe equipment under realistic operating conditions. This balance of physical crafting, engineering analysis, and direct contextual observation keeps our design work grounded in practical human utility.',
	'st_p1_n' => 'Ines Varga',
	'st_p1_r' => 'Founder and design director',
	'st_p1_t' => 'Founded the studio in 2011 and directs every design programme, medical and consumer.',
	'st_p2_n' => 'Kofi Asante',
	'st_p2_r' => 'Head of model shop',
	'st_p2_t' => 'Leads the Haverholt workshop: foam shaping, precision sanding and resin appearance prints.',
	'st_p3' => 'Many design consultancies scale by adding junior staff, which inevitably delegates crucial CAD modeling and workshop testing away from experienced directors. We believe that exceptional industrial design and medical device engineering require deep, uninterrupted concentration from seasoned practitioners. By capping our studio at nine projects a year—and never running more than four active tooling programs simultaneously—we ensure that Ines Varga, Mateo Ruiz, and our senior specialists personally handle every phase. This deliberate constraint ensures our clients receive direct, accountable leadership from initial workshop discovery until the first production parts leave the manufacturing tool.',
